---
{* No props - the navbar reads $cart from the render context. *}
---

{*
  {$let} seeds CLIENT state and must sit in the BODY, not in frontmatter:
  frontmatter only accepts directives, and an unrecognised statement there is
  silently discarded, so this line emitted nothing at all when it lived above.

  In the body it compiles to a JSON payload the browser runtime picks up:
    <script type="application/json" data-slurp-let="menuOpen">false</script>

  It creates NO server-side binding. ${ menuOpen } renders empty here and
  {if menuOpen} is always false, so the markup below is written to render in
  its CLOSED state and to be opened by the runtime toggling a class.
*}
{$let menuOpen = false}

<nav class="navbar">
  <div class="navbar__inner">

    {* Logo. Quote the numbers: unquoted width=120 lexes as an attribute NAME
       and the value is silently dropped. *}
    <a href="/" class="navbar__logo" aria-label="Go to homepage">
      <img src="/logo.svg" alt="Our Store" width="120" height="36" />
    </a>

    {* Desktop nav links *}
    <ul class="navbar__links" role="list">
      <li><a href="/" class="navbar__link">Home</a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/all" class="navbar__link">Collections</a></li>
      <li><a href="/about" class="navbar__link">About</a></li>
    </ul>

    {* Cart icon with reactive badge *}
    <a href="/cart" class="navbar__cart" aria-label="View cart">
      <svg class="navbar__cart-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
        <circle cx="9" cy="21" r="1" />
        <circle cx="20" cy="21" r="1" />
        <path d="M1 1h4l2.68 13.39a2 2 0 0 0 2 1.61h9.72a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.61L23 6H6" />
      </svg>
      {if $cart.count > 0}
        <span class="navbar__cart-badge" aria-live="polite">${ $cart.count }</span>
      {/if}
    </a>

    {*
      Mobile menu toggle.

      on:click compiles to a LITERAL on:click attribute. Slurp itself never
      binds it, and neither does @bytesell/slurp-runtime - it is a declaration for a
      host runtime to pick up. It is also not interpolated: unlike an ordinary
      attribute, a ${ } inside an on: value is passed through verbatim.

      aria-expanded is written as a literal "false" rather than ${ menuOpen },
      because {$let} state is not readable server-side and would render the
      attribute empty. "false" is the correct SERVER-rendered starting state.
    *}
    <button
      class={
        "navbar__toggle",
        "navbar__toggle--open": menuOpen
      }
      on:click="menuOpen = !menuOpen"
      aria-expanded="false"
      aria-controls="mobile-menu"
      aria-label="Toggle navigation"
    >
      <span class="navbar__toggle-bar"></span>
      <span class="navbar__toggle-bar"></span>
      <span class="navbar__toggle-bar"></span>
    </button>
  </div>

  {*
    Mobile menu.

    This was written as {if menuOpen} ... {/if}, which can never render: the
    condition is evaluated ONCE on the server, where menuOpen is null, so the
    menu was absent from the HTML entirely and no client toggle could ever
    reveal it. An {if} is not a reactive region - it is decided at render time
    and baked into the output.

    So the markup is always emitted, in its closed state, and opening it is a
    matter of the --open class. CSS hides it by default.
  *}
  <div
    id="mobile-menu"
    class={
      "navbar__mobile",
      "navbar__mobile--open": menuOpen
    }
  >
    <ul role="list">
      <li><a href="/" class="navbar__link" on:click="menuOpen = false">Home</a></li>
      <li><a href="/collections/all" class="navbar__link" on:click="menuOpen = false">Collections</a></li>
      <li><a href="/about" class="navbar__link" on:click="menuOpen = false">About</a></li>
      <li><a href="/cart" class="navbar__link" on:click="menuOpen = false">Cart (${ $cart.count })</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

<style>
.navbar {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 100;
  background: #fff;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
}
.navbar__inner {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 1.5rem;
  max-width: 1280px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 1.5rem;
  height: 4rem;
}
.navbar__logo { margin-right: auto; }
.navbar__links {
  display: flex;
  gap: 1.5rem;
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}
.navbar__link {
  color: #374151;
  text-decoration: none;
  font-weight: 500;
}
.navbar__link:hover { color: #111827; }
.navbar__cart {
  position: relative;
  color: #374151;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
}
.navbar__cart-badge {
  position: absolute;
  top: -0.5rem;
  right: -0.5rem;
  background: #111827;
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 0.65rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  min-width: 1.1rem;
  height: 1.1rem;
  border-radius: 9999px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  padding: 0 0.2rem;
}
.navbar__toggle {
  display: none;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 4px;
  background: none;
  border: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  padding: 0.25rem;
}
.navbar__toggle-bar {
  display: block;
  width: 22px;
  height: 2px;
  background: #374151;
  border-radius: 2px;
  transition: transform 0.2s;
}
.navbar__mobile {
  display: none;
  border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
}
.navbar__mobile--open { display: block; }
.navbar__mobile ul {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.75rem;
}
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .navbar__links { display: none; }
  .navbar__toggle { display: flex; }
}
</style>
